# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/

# uv
# uv.lock IS committed — it is the reproducibility guarantee.

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Local data — captures and databases never enter the repository
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backend/data/
captures/

# Datasets and model artefacts are DVC-tracked, not git-tracked
dataset/**/*.pcap
dataset/**/*.pcapng
# Generated sessions: a batch run writes a labels.json and a manifest.json
# beside every capture, and 200 of those would otherwise land in a `git add -A`
# even though the captures beside them are ignored. Step 8.4 puts the whole
# tree under DVC.
dataset/sessions/

# dataset/demo/ is the exception, and it is committed on purpose.
#
# Step 11.5's Done-when is that the two PRD 16 demo captures are *committed*
# and that neither appears in any training split. Both halves need this rule:
# committed, so a clone can run the demo without a testbed and without DVC; and
# outside dataset/sessions/, so `load_dataset` cannot walk them into a fold.
# 6.6 MB for the two, which is the price of a demo that works from a fresh
# clone. See backend/testbed/demo_captures.py.
!dataset/demo/
!dataset/demo/**

backend/models/*.pkl
backend/models/*.joblib
backend/models/*.onnx
backend/models/*.pt
# The artefacts inference loads are committed, all 3.3 MB of them: the
# LightGBM traffic and mode classifiers, their feature/label order, and the
# isotonic calibration knots. DVC would be the right home for model weights
# and this project documents it as such -- but no DVC remote is configured, so
# ignoring them means a teammate's clone has no models, cannot train without
# the 14 GB dataset that is also not in git, and silently loses every Track B
# inference to UNAVAILABLE. A few megabytes in git beats a broken checkout.
#
# `traffic_cnn.pt` stays out: inference deliberately loads LightGBM rather than
# the CNN so that torch is not a runtime dependency (see models/README.md), so
# the checkpoint is a training artefact that no deployment reads.
backend/models/*.pt

# The batch logs of a generation run. Several megabytes of per-session INFO
# lines whose useful content is already summarised in CHANGELOG.md.
dataset/gen*.log
dataset/pilot*.log
dataset/verify.log
dataset/train.log

# metrics.json, reliability_cnn.json and external_validation.json are NOT
# ignored, deliberately. They are the *measurements* -- what the models scored
# and on what -- and they are what docs/model-card.md is generated from. The
# weights are reproducible from the dataset; the record of what they achieved
# on a particular held-out fold is not, and losing it would leave a model card
# nobody could check.

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# npm on Windows occasionally materialises its cache under the reserved name NUL
NUL/

# The retraining and regeneration logs of the second Phase 8/9 run. `gen*.log`
# above already covers the originals; these follow the same rule — the logs are
# provenance for a run, not for the repository.
dataset/train2.log
dataset/demo-gen.log
dataset/regen-msg-*.log
